Chapter 5 built upon a lot of subjects I have studied in the past. It made me recall learning the basics of the scientific method, particularly hypothesis and dependent and independent variables. The chapter helped me make the connection of why it is important to form a hypothesis before research, as well as what a theory is and how theory contributes to research. Theory is like the lens that you view the research topic through, so it can help determine research methods. The section that described theories helped me make the connection to the theories I studied when I took Mass Media in Society. One of those theories was uses and gratifications theory, and seeing it applied to the Twitch data gave me a better understanding of the theory. I think a few of the theories can apply to my chosen topic of how social media users interact with influencer advertising versus advertising that doesn't involve influencers. For example, according to the social identity theory, an influencer's followers may buy products they promote because they want to identify with that influencer or identify with the influencer's circle, social group, etc. Similarly, parasocial interaction theory would be a good lens through which to study consumer behavior around influencer marketing because it predicts that followers form one-sided connections with influencers that can influence their purchasing behaviors.
